ignatures, replay, set, sorted\n- L164--186 `def bounded_bfs(env, goal_fn, actions: Sequence[int] = (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE), key_fn=None, max_states: int = 20000, max_depth: int = 80):` — Generic clone BFS over observational keys. Use small max_states first.; calls: arr, deque, goal_fn, int, key_fn, len\n- L189--229 `def bounded_replay_bfs(env, goal_fn, action_fn, key_fn=None, max_states: int = 20000, max_depth: int = 80):` — Path-only BFS for games whose deep Arena clones become expensive.; calls: action_fn, arr, deque, goal_fn, int, isinstance, key_fn, len, reconstruct\n- L232--233 `def level_goal(base_level: int):`\n\n## solve.py\n- L3--13 `def solve(env): # dispatch to the per-level player for the current level, in a loop`; calls: fn, getattr\n# Unverified frontier brief: tu93 level 4\n\nThis is a compact index of the latest clean WIP, not solver evidence.\nReproduce every observation you rely on with the documented local API.\nDo not reread the full proposer transcript unless a named ambiguity requires it.\n\n## Prior proposer progress\n\n- I’ll stay strictly inside the workspace and begin with the indexed API surface, then reproduce any frontier observations before probing level 3. I’ll keep frame analysis symbolic and clone searches bounded.\n- Baseline is confirmed at level 3 (`levels=2`, 28 committed moves). Next I’m inspecting only the harness entry points and the indexed perception helpers needed to construct a level-3 clone, then I’ll identify the moving object and action semantics experimentally.\n- The moving 3×3 object is the avatar (color 9 with a one-pixel facing marker); actions map to cardinal movement, with action 1 moving it one maze node upward. Level 3 is the same block-maze substrate but now has three color-8 directional nodes plus the color-14 goal. I’m reproducing the known level-2 directional marker to decode the three required approaches, then I’ll verify each traversal on clones.\n- The directional rule is now verified in two contexts: a marker on the left edge requires entering upward, and a marker on the right edge requires entering downward; correct entry removes that waypoint while leaving the others intact. This supports a general rotated-marker decoder. I’m adding one reusable multi-waypoint maze leg whose dense progress measure is the number of remaining color-8 marker blocks, with the color-14 goal held back until that count reaches zero.\n- The first implementation correctly began the route but stalled after four live steps, so I’m not treating the directional hypothesis as sufficient yet. I’m tracing the replanner’s symbolic state—avatar node, remaining markers, and next planned action—on a clone to isolate whether the issue is reachability blocking or marker decoding after the avatar turns.\n- The trace exposed an important correction: the color-8 objects are not static gates. One moves from its node into the avatar’s node when the avatar reaches the adjacent cell, confirming context-dependent interaction. I’m switching from the static-waypoint model to a bounded clone search keyed by the visible board (excluding the depleting HUD row); its winning traces will let me compare the exact interaction sequence against non-winning collisions before generalizing the leg.\n- The bounded search found a 19-move win after only 114 visible states. Its dense trace is decisive: the marker count drops `3→2→1→0`, then entering the color-14 goal raises the level. It also corrected the last mapping: a bottom-edge marker means enter rightward (not leftward). I’m updating the general decoder and validating the composed player end to end.\n- End-to-end validation now passes exactly as the winning clone predicted: `RESULT levels=3 moves=47 replay_ok=True` (28 prior-level moves + 19 for level 3). The missing constraint was reachability around each marker-facing trigger cell; avoiding those cells prevents premature object motion, while correct entries reduce the marker count to zero. I’m removing the temporary probes and doing a final syntax plus replay check.\n- Implemented level 3 using reusable legs: - Added directional-marker maze planning in [legs.py](/Users/sasha/gkm/arc/crack_lab/runs/scratch/gkm_legs_ws_tu93_budgeted_medium_screen/legs.py:201). - Added the composed level player in [players.py](/Users/sasha/gkm/arc/crack_lab/runs/scratch/gkm_legs_ws_tu93_budgeted_medium_screen/players.py:15). - Removed temporary probe scripts. Final verification: ```text RESULT levels=3 moves=47 replay_ok=True err=None ``` Syntax compilation also passes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
